    <string name="predictive_alert_safety_section">Safety</string>
    <string name="predictive_alert_safety_title">Guidance, not a treatment instruction</string>
    <string name="predictive_alert_safety_body">Forecasts can be wrong or delayed. This feature never calculates insulin or carbohydrate amounts. Check glucose and follow your agreed care plan.</string>
    <string name="predictive_alert_shadow_body">Predictive alerts are an additional safety layer. After a predictive warning is successfully posted, the legacy early warning is paused for that direction and active episode while the forecast stays fresh, approved, and postable. If data, service, permission, channel, or local calibration makes delivery unavailable, that legacy early warning remains active. Current low, high and signal-loss alarms are never changed.</string>
    <string name="predictive_alert_legacy_disabled_hint">Legacy early-warning settings remain available. A direction is handed over only after its predictive warning was successfully posted and only for that active episode.</string>

